WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:09.661
Welcome, arcade engineer! Today you’ll learn how games make dozens of enemies, coins and raindrops from just one sprite.

2
00:00:10.261 --> 00:00:16.713
A clone is a copy of a sprite, made while the program runs.

3
00:00:16.713 --> 00:00:23.165
One Star sprite can make ten falling stars without you drawing ten sprites.

4
00:00:23.765 --> 00:00:30.217
Every new clone runs the script under “when I start as a clone”.

5
00:00:30.217 --> 00:00:36.670
Each clone can go to its own random place and move by itself.

6
00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:43.722
Usually the original sprite hides and just makes clones — like a factory.

7
00:00:43.722 --> 00:00:47.565
Each clone shows itself when it starts.

8
00:00:48.165 --> 00:00:55.052
Delete clones when they are finished (for example, when they fall off the bottom).

9
00:00:55.052 --> 00:01:00.635
Too many clones slow a game down — Scratch allows 300.

10
00:01:01.235 --> 00:01:05.078
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

11
00:01:05.078 --> 00:01:10.226
Now build along, then try the challenges. You’ve got this!
